Enable CONFIG_BTRFS_EXPERIMENTAL for the out-of-tree btrfs build.

This is the ONLY change made to the upstream fs/btrfs tree. It unlocks the
raid-stripe-tree (RST) incompat feature, which is otherwise excluded from
BTRFS_FEATURE_INCOMPAT_SUPP unless CONFIG_BTRFS_EXPERIMENTAL is defined at
compile time (see fs/fs.h).

Apply from the root of a fs/btrfs source tree with:  patch -p1 < this-file

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+subdir-ccflags-y += -DCONFIG_BTRFS_EXPERIMENTAL
 
 # Subset of W=1 warnings
 subdir-ccflags-y += -Wextra -Wunused -Wno-unused-parameter
 subdir-ccflags-y += -Wmissing-declarations
